# Force TodoWrite for plan execution

Multi-step work and Cursor Plan builds MUST track progress with the `TodoWrite` tool. Plan markdown checkboxes alone are not enough.

## When required

Use `TodoWrite` whenever you:

- Execute a scaffolded plan / Plan Mode build
- Work through 2+ distinct implementation steps
- Follow a bullet list of tasks from the user

## Required workflow

1. At start: create the full todo list with `TodoWrite` (one item per plan point). Prefer `merge: true` for later updates.
2. Set exactly one item to `in_progress` while working on it.
3. As soon as that point is done, mark it `completed` with `TodoWrite` **before** starting the next point.
4. Never batch-complete several points in one TodoWrite call after the fact.
5. Do not skip TodoWrite because a Plan file already has to-dos — mirror those points into TodoWrite and keep TodoWrite as the live status source.

## Why

A project hook commits (unsigned, no push) after each newly completed TodoWrite item. If you do not call TodoWrite, those commits will not happen.

## Examples

```text
✅ GOOD
TodoWrite: create [A, B, C] → work A → TodoWrite A=completed, B=in_progress → work B → ...

❌ BAD
Finish A and B in code, only update the Plan markdown, never call TodoWrite

❌ BAD
Finish all points, then one TodoWrite marking everything completed
```